WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.300
-The charades champion.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.334
-Right?
-Yes! We are the champs.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:07.434
-Not deserved at all.
-No, not at all. No, not at all.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:08.634
But, by the way,
you kept saying,

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:09.868
"Hey, we're going to come back.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.234
We're going to come back."
And what did we do?

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:12.501
-Exactly.
-Came back. Unbelievable.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:15.701
Yeah, I want to talk about this,
"Dear Evan Hansen."

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:16.801
-Yeah.
-You're coming back to Broadway.

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:19.267
-I am.
-Are you --

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you very much.

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:23.801
Is it like riding a bike?

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.968
Do you go, "Oh, I know how to
do this -- Broadway"?

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:26.968
-A little bit.

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:29.968
It's more -- So,
if that's riding a bike,

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:32.601
this is kind of like
getting on a motorcycle.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:33.901
-Oh, it is?

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:36.501
-Yeah, a little bit,
just because I haven't been --

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.434
I haven't run in
a show long term,

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:39.901
consistently since I was 12,

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.667
and that was before
my voice changed.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.601
I was only doing
four shows a week then.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.000
Now I'm doing eight.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.234
-I can just imagine it's just so
straining on your voice to do --

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.834
-Especially --
Yeah, this show is

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:55.634
not kind to most of
the performers in it.

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:58.100
And I'm playing Jared.
I'm very, very excited.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.501
And --
-Wow! When does it begin?

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:01.901
When do you --

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.534
-I open July 19th.
-Wow!

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:05.801
-Yeah.
-That's soon.

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.133
It is soon.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.334
-That whole cast of
"Stranger Things" can all sing.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:10.968
-A good portion, yes.
-It's, like, a talented cast.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.234
-Some of them much better
than I can, yeah.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.834
-Remember, I think, Season 1,
do you remember

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.534
that you were doing this thing
that all the rest of

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:18.200
the cast was getting annoyed by.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.634
You kept singing, "Oh, my God"?

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.901
-[ Laughs ]
-Do you remember this?

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.334
-♪ Oh, my God ♪
Yeah, that one.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:26.534
-Yeah, yeah,
You kept saying, "Oh, my God."

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.934
And everyone was like,
"Will you stop saying that?"

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.601
But that was your
catchphrase at the time.

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.033
-At the time, yeah.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:35.501
I wanted something that, like,
they'd hear just in the distance

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:37.400
and they'd be like,
"Oh, there he is."

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.033
-Yeah.
Can you do it one more time?

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:40.400
-♪ Oh, my God ♪

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.367
I was better at it
when I was like 14.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:43.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:46.267
I was better --
-No, it's so good.

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:47.334
That should be --
Someone should sample that

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:48.434
and put it in a song.

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:50.667
-Well, it's better when
The Roots can

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:51.968
accompany you with it.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:54.167
-Can you do a little bit of a...
♪♪

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:56.300
-Yeah.
-[ Humming ]

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.434
-♪ Oh, my God ♪

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:01.534
-Yeah.
-Yeah, of course. It's perfect.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:02.934
-♪ Oh, my God ♪

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:05.234
-Yeah.
That's what we need, yeah.

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:07.501
-In the show,
I guess I got to see

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.734
"NeverEnding Story," of course.

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.667
-Yeah.
-We'll get to that.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.000
"Running Up That Hill,"
by the way.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.501
How about that?
-Right?

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:14.834
-That's taking
a life of its own.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.901
-It's great for me.
-Yeah.

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:19.200
-Because it's replaced
"NeverEnding Story."

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.033
-Oh, because
that was your thing.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.567
-Oh, yeah. That was --

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.100
-We've done stuff with you on
the show where like,

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.434
"Do you mind doing that?"

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:30.234
But now it's on Sadie's --
-Now it's sucks for Sadie.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:33.701
Yeah. But I'm in the clear
for a bit.

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:34.834
It's awesome.

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:37.467
-Did you like hearing it,
like, when you're

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:38.734
doing it on the show?

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.434
-I love doing it on the show.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:43.167
-Gabby, who plays Suzie,
is just awesome and incredible.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.501
And she's a Broadway kid,
as well.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:45.567
-Really?

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.000
-Yeah, she was
in "Fun Home" for like --

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.400
I just saw her.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.901
Like three or four years,
she ran in that show,

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.834
which is a really long time,

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:57.534
especially for a kid actor.

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:58.734
Yeah, but she's great.

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:00.534
And when she came on set,
we like heard it like

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.067
10 minutes before we shot.

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:04.501
And then we, like,
got a harmony track set up

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:05.868
and all that jazz, yeah.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:07.634
-It was greatest.
-It was fun.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:10.300
-When Sadie was on the show,
she was --

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.000
I was talking about Vecna
was the new character

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.067
who has, like, kind of
taken off a little bit.

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:15.100
-Catch up.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.868
-Yeah, that show,
"Stranger Things," yeah.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:18.801
Here's Vecna.
And she said she had a very --

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:19.901
-There he is.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.601
-I go, "Was he frightening
on the set?

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.367
And she goes, "Actually, no,
because I had --

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:27.334
My first time I met Vecna,
he was eating a sandwich."

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:29.200
-Yeah.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.767
-Kind of takes
all the frightening out

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:31.901
as he's eating a hoagie.

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.334
Just chomping on a hoagie.

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:38.033
-It reminds -- I saw him once
during filming of Volume 1.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.968
I saw him at -- Like one time.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:43.100
And we were doing, like --

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:46.234
I was in costume,
and we were doing 3-D scans.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:47.767
Like, you have to go into your
room and, like --

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:49.534
They, like, take a bunch of
pictures all around,

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:50.834
'cause there's a lot of
animation in the show,

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.167
especially this year.

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.534
And so it was kind of, like,
a little line of, like,

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.667
the cast, like, in costume,

00:03:56.667 --> 00:04:00.901
like, they went -- whenever they
had free time during filming.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:04.300
And I saw --
-Vecna?

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.133
-Yeah.
I saw Vecna sitting there.

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:08.534
And I looked over.

00:04:08.534 --> 00:04:10.334
I was like,
"Hi. it's great to see you."

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.667
I hadn't seen him
since the table read.

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:14.100
And he was just like,
"Yeah, how are you?

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.267
It's good to see you."

00:04:15.267 --> 00:04:18.033
Like, just in a lawn chair,
like, feet up,

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:20.868
and, like, whole half, like,
done up in Vecna gear.

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:25.000
It is unsettling
and just bonkers, yeah.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.467
-From the waist down wearing,
like, sweatpants?

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.667
-Yeah, pretty much, I think.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:29.934
I think,
if I remember correctly.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:33.067
I was kind of drawn towards
his messed-up face.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:34.634
But --

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:36.634
-And he's just talking to you
like he's not Vecna?

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:37.701
-Yeah, it was like,
"How are you?"

00:04:37.701 --> 00:04:38.834
He's like,
"It's good to see you."

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:41.367
Like, he looked exhausted.
-That reminds me.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:42.601
We did a bit,
The Roots and I did,

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:44.033
at Macy's Thanksgiving Day
Parade.

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.067
And we're on the float
and we're on a bus.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.167
You know, they put all the
people that are going to be on

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.100
the floats on a bus
before you go on the float.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.300
And, so, it was me and The Roots
and Ronald McDonald.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.667
And it's just great.
The guy was so nice.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.067
But he's dressed like
Ronald McDonald.

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:00.868
-But he's Ronald McDonald.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.133
-Yeah, and he's having
a normal conversation,

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:03.334
like, drinking a coffee.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.601
He's like, "Yeah, man,
the subway was crazy."

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:08.434
I go, "I can't have --
You're Ronald McDonald."

00:05:08.434 --> 00:05:10.300
-Did you laugh?
-No.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.033
No, I just had to tell him,
"You've got to stop,

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:14.434
because, like, you're dressed
like Ronald McDonald."

00:05:14.434 --> 00:05:15.601
-I wouldn't have been
able to breathe.

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:17.534
-Had a full-on hour-and-a-half
conversation

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:18.601
with Ronald McDonald.

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:19.801
And we were all freaking out.

00:05:19.801 --> 00:05:21.601
We're like, "Oh, my gosh."
And then, James --

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:23.467
-Of course you have, like,
the -- you're doing the parade.

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:24.968
That's pretty
nerve-racking, right?

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:26.267
-Yeah.
We were nervous about that.

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.167
But then we were all kind of
just freaking out that

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:29.634
Ronald McDonald
was on the thing.

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:31.734
And we're like -- And James
was about to come on the bus,

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:33.167
and we're like,
"Oh, James is going freak out

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.834
that we're talking to
Ronald McDonald."

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.267
And James came on the bus.

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:37.701
Do you remember
what he said, Quest?

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:40.000
-Yeah. He was like,
"What's up, Ron?"

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.634
-He said, "What's up, Ron?"
like he's one of our friends.

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:46.701
It was like, we're sitting
talking to Ronald McDonald.

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:50.334
James is going -- And he goes,
"What's up, Ron?"

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:52.267
Like him and Ronald McDonald
hang out or something.

00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:53.334
-What is it -- What are, like,

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:55.067
the daily issues
of Ronald McDonald?

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:56.701
Like, what are like the --

00:05:56.701 --> 00:06:00.834
-Putting curlers
in the wig, yeah.

00:06:00.834 --> 00:06:02.434
He's got kind of
a curled hairstyle.

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:03.868
-Yeah.
-He's got big shoes.

00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:05.067
-Beautifully coiffed.

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:06.767
-He's got a coif,
Ronald McDonald.

00:06:06.767 --> 00:06:08.200
Got the yellow jodhpurs.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.634
-It's a lot.
Shoes are a bit big.

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:12.033
-Shoes are giantly big.
He's dressed like a clown.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:14.601
-Sure.
-He's a pretty famous clown.

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:19.400
I mean, he has to take, like,
a car to wherever he's going.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.601
He can't take
public transportation.

00:06:20.601 --> 00:06:21.968
-No.

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:23.567
-You know?
-I guess not, yeah.

00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:25.801
I never thought about the
struggles of being

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:27.968
Ronald McDonald,
though, I go to say.

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:29.734
-There's got to be a documentary
there somewhere.

00:06:29.734 --> 00:06:30.834
-Yeah.

00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:32.868
-What goes on --
I mean, it's like Vecna.

00:06:32.868 --> 00:06:34.000
It's like Vecna.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.300
The poor guy
can't even eat a sandwich.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.868
-He can't go anywhere.

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:40.033
-He can't be on his cellphone,
checking his voicemail.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:42.434
Can't go to Starbucks.
He's like, "Ah, I'm Vecna."

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:45.100
-"No, I got big [bleep] to do."

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.868
-Yeah. "I got
big things to do," yeah.

00:06:46.868 --> 00:06:49.467
Season 4, Volume 2
comes out this Friday.

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:50.934
-Yeah.
-I know you've done --

00:06:50.934 --> 00:06:53.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:53.434 --> 00:06:56.901
You've done a great job
not giving any spoilers away,

00:06:56.901 --> 00:06:58.133
and I'm not
going to get you in trouble.

00:06:58.133 --> 00:06:59.267
-Thank you.

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:01.801
-I just want to --
This is your wardrobe.

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:05.200
-Yeah. That's great. That's fun.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.567
-Yeah. Okay, so I'm assuming
that there is some --

00:07:07.567 --> 00:07:09.434
there's a big finale.

00:07:09.434 --> 00:07:11.067
-Yeah, as you can see.
-Yes.

00:07:11.067 --> 00:07:13.334
There's also -- Here's you --
-There's a picture.

00:07:13.334 --> 00:07:15.133
I look so cute
in that picture, don't I?

00:07:15.133 --> 00:07:16.367
-You look so cute here.
Yeah. Oh, my God.

00:07:16.367 --> 00:07:17.868
This should be
the poster for it.

00:07:17.868 --> 00:07:20.734
-That's the new Instagram
bio pic right there.

00:07:20.734 --> 00:07:22.868
-But when you're doing this,

00:07:22.868 --> 00:07:24.300
you go, "Okay, Oh, my gosh.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.667
We have -- They go, "Oh, there's
two new episodes coming out."

00:07:26.667 --> 00:07:28.801
And you go, "Yeah."
They go, "Oh, two? That's it?"

00:07:28.801 --> 00:07:30.634
And you go, "No."

00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:33.300
Every episode is like -- The
first episode's like two hours?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.267
-The first episode --
so eighth episode is,

00:07:35.267 --> 00:07:36.968
I think,
probably an hour and a half.

00:07:36.968 --> 00:07:40.133
But Episode 9 is getting
close to 2 1/2 hours.

00:07:40.133 --> 00:07:41.234
It's a movie.

00:07:41.234 --> 00:07:43.300
-That is a movie
right there coming out.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.033
-I know.
-You did a movie.

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:46.434
They're all kind of
beautifully done.

00:07:46.434 --> 00:07:50.968
-They're basically just --
It's nine movies, practically.

00:07:50.968 --> 00:07:53.300
All of them are close to
an hour and a half.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.467
All of them over an hour.
-They're so good.

00:07:55.467 --> 00:07:57.267
And it's all
starting to pay off.

00:07:57.267 --> 00:07:58.934
And everything works
and it's really cool.

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:00.968
-Yeah, we definitely --
You learn a lot.

00:08:00.968 --> 00:08:02.100
-You learn a lot, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.634
-And it's a scary and it's good.
-Yeah.

00:08:03.634 --> 00:08:04.968
-Yeah.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:04.968 --> 00:08:07.934
Here's Gaten Matarazzo in
Season 4 of "Stranger Things."

00:08:07.934 --> 00:08:09.367
Take a look at this.

00:08:09.367 --> 00:08:11.334
-Hey, Steve.

00:08:11.334 --> 00:08:12.601
-Did you guys see this?
-How many phones do you have?

00:08:12.601 --> 00:08:13.801
-Someone was murdered.

00:08:13.801 --> 00:08:16.767
-How many phones do you have?
-Uh, two. Why?

00:08:16.767 --> 00:08:18.734
-Uh, technically three if you
count Keith's in the back.

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:20.567
-Yeah, three works.

00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:22.033
-What are you doing?

00:08:22.033 --> 00:08:23.634
Whoa! What are you --
-My pile!

00:08:23.634 --> 00:08:25.701
-No, no, no, no! Not my tapes!

00:08:25.701 --> 00:08:28.167
Dude! What are you doing, man?

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:29.434
-Setting up
base of operations here.

00:08:29.434 --> 00:08:30.934
-Base of operations?

00:08:30.934 --> 00:08:32.000
-Stop. Get off of that.
-No. I need it.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.167
-Need it for what?

00:08:33.167 --> 00:08:34.200
-Looking up Eddie's friends'
phone numbers.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.367
-Oh, Eddie.

00:08:35.367 --> 00:08:36.567
Your new best friend, Eddie,
who you think

00:08:36.567 --> 00:08:37.968
is cooler than me because
